  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "4",
  "quote": "a provision in a tenancy agreement that is inconsistent with this Act or the regulations is void",
  "reason": "Sections 121 and 126 of the Act give the landlord the statutory right to increase rent above the guideline by agreement with the tenant or by order of the Board. Because this clause attempts to contract out of and prohibit those statutory mechanisms for above-guideline rent increases, it is inconsistent with the Act and void under section 4."
}

